      <title>A New Steel Plant in Iowa Shows the Lunacy of Trump's Tariff Policy</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-08/a-new-steel-plant-in-iowa-shows-the-lunacy-of-trump-s-tariff-policy</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">316cd1e52515bdb166a75f8e</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:30:22 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>With great fanfare, President Donald Trump announced last week that “the largest steel plant ever built in the United States” would be coming to Lee County, Iowa, adding that Mesabi Metallics’ $15 billion investment in a pivotal midterm swing state proved his “powerful 50% tariffs” were working.  He’s right: The announcement is a tangible result of American steel policy — but, contrary to what the president said, that’s not a good thing.</description>
      <dc:creator>Scott Lincicome</dc:creator>
